From 44e4a00ce97ba0998215d02f08b1d92aa11f25b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:07:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 88/89] render: volumetric point and spot lights
 (castvolumetrics)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A light with `castvolumetrics` (flags +0x2c4 bit 2; `density` +0x2f8 default 2,
`volumetricsscattering` +0x2fc 0.5, `volumetricsexponent` +0x300 1: GH 0x140283df0's table, the
factory's defaults) is marched as wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485's volumetrics pass (GH 0x1401c56e0)
does, with WE's own materials and shaders: per light its volume's back faces' depth into
_rt_volumetricsSingle (volumetrics_back), then its front faces (volumetrics_front), or a
full-screen quad while the eye's probe (eye + forward · 0.2) is inside it (volumetrics_fullscreen),
march from the front face to the nearer of the back face and the scene's depth (_rt_volumetricsBack)
into _rt_volumetricsLightBuffer (additive, an eighth of the scene at the default medium quality,
GH 0x140048ca0), blurred by blur_k3 across and down through _rt_volumetricsLightBufferB and added
to the scene (volumetrics_combine). The volume is a 32-segment cone in the spot's clip space
(GH 0x140282d40) or a sphere of the point light's radius; g_RenderVar1..4 are packed as WE does
(radius · 0.99, cos inner, cos outer, intensity; origin, density; the spot's x axis;
colour · scattering, volumetricsexponent), QUALITY 2, POINTLIGHT for a point light.

Ours: the volumetricsfront shader compares GL depth-texture values with D3D-style clip depth, so
the front pass draws through the view-projection with z remapped to 0 … w and unprojects through
its inverse; the depth targets are y-flipped (the shader's screen uv grows down): the scene's depth
is blitted flipped, the back faces drawn through a y-flipped view-projection (which also turns
them to the material's culling). Light buffers are half float. sampler2DBackBuffer annotations
parse as samplers. Not done: SHADOW and COOKIE volumetrics, fog in the march, directional
volumetrics (2.8.485's volumetrics_directional, not in 2.8.42's assets), the quality setting.
Where WE runs the pass in the frame is inferred (after the objects, before the fade).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "F2 result" (batch F2, castvolumetrics)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
